<title>USA: Weekend U.S. box office chart -- Nov 22-24.</title>
<headline>Weekend U.S. box office chart -- Nov 22-24.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the final data for the top 10 movies at the November 22-24 U.S. box office, according to Exhibitor Relations Co.</p>
<p>    Film		   Three-day gross    Cumulative Gross</p>
<p>1. Star Trek:</p>
<p>    First Contact	   $30,716,131	 $  ----</p>
<p>2. Space Jam		  $16,216,845	 $ 48,276,267</p>
<p>3. Ransom		     $13,185,106	 $ 85,745,878</p>
<p>4. Jingle All The Way     $12,112,267	 $  ----</p>
<p>5. The Mirror Has  </p>
<p>    Two Faces		 $ 8,012,555	 $ 24,095,577</p>
<p>6. Set It Off		 $ 3,322,947	 $ 25,521,726</p>
<p>7. Romeo &amp; Juliet	   $ 3,195,515	 $ 35,816,436</p>
<p>8. The English Patient    $ 2,713,093	 $  3,205,999</p>
<p>9. Sleepers		   $ 1,369,471	 $ 49,138,306</p>
<p>10 The First Wives Club   $   723,675	 $100,577,663</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;Star Trek: First Contact&quot; and &quot;The First Wives Club&quot; are released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc.. &quot;Space Jam&quot; and &quot;Sleepers&quot; are released by Warner Bros., a unit of Time Warner Inc.. &quot;Ransom&quot; is released by Walt Disney Co.. &quot;Jingle All The Way&quot; and &quot;William Shakespeare's Romeo and Juliet&quot; are released by News Corp.'s 20th Century Fox. &quot;The Mirror Has Two Faces&quot; is released by Sony Corp.. &quot;Set It Off&quot; is released by New Line Cinema, a unit of Time Warner. &quot;The English Patient&quot; is released by Disney's Miramax Films unit.</p>
